darkroom_ai
Third-party attribution

Parts of the design and logic of darkroom_ai's mask handling were ported (re-implemented in
Lua and Python, behind darkroom_ai's own safety checks) from the pure Lightroom SDK portions of:

  lightroom-mcp by par4987 (a fork of Automaat/lightroom-mcp by Marcin Skalski)
  https://github.com/par4987/lightroom-mcp
  Licensed under the MIT License.

What was taken: the way masks are created through the SDK (including the need to verify success by
diffing the mask list, and the asynchronous AI step), the way local adjustments are read and written
as a stored table, and the idea of confirming a write with a small throwaway render. Nothing that
runs PowerShell, sends keystrokes or captures the screen was taken.

